it's only the start of fire season in  the amazon  but it's already the worst in a decade  brazil's national institute for space  research is reporting a total of 6  300 blazes in july 28 percent more than  for the same period  in 2019 environment minister hikaru  sales  says measures are being taken to prevent  last year's tragedy from repeating  itself  we are sending an additional 3 000  firefighters and more aircrafts to  protect the forests and prevent their  destruction  in july the government banned fires for  120 days in the amazon and bandana  regions  farmers have been forbidden from burning  vegetation to clear their land during  the dry season  but that hasn't stopped them it took one  farmer in the northern state of para  half an hour to clear his land  by the time satellites and local  authorities spotted the  fire it was too late  we perform a satellite analysis which  gives us information about where these  infractions are taking place  and based on that we search the system  and also identify  who owns this area while president  bolsonaro has been criticized for  downplaying the fires  the government is on a public relations  campaign to prevent a repeat of last  year's global backlash  especially after investors threaten to  divest if brazil fails to curb  environmental destruction last year  bolsonaro falsely accused actor  and environmentalist leonardo dicaprio  of funding  fires in the amazon rainforest this year  brazil's vice president amir tomorrow  invited the hollywood actor for an  eight-hour march in the jungle  so he could see for himself how  difficult  it is to protect such a huge area  morale has deployed thousands of  military to protect the rain forest  but the local kaiapa indigenous tribe  already fearful of kovit 19  say they feel far from safe believing  the fires as much as a threat  as the disease monika yanakiv al-jazeera  rio de janeiro
 

